Black Hole Journey — Pictogram Motion (Lemo-Opuscar)
A 4:18 explainer: what it would actually be like to fall into a black hole —
the bend in the sky, the accretion disk, spaghettification, the event horizon,
the frozen outside view, the singularity, and the slow leak of Hawking radiation.
Twenty shots in six chapters; grown from the 30-second style sample (films/sample-pictogram).
All drawings, lettering layout, animation, sound effects and music are original and generated by code in this folder.

MUSIC (music/score.py, original composition, 120 BPM, D minor)
Marimba, vibraphone (bowed), glass, electric bass, violins (tremolo), timpani, crash —
sample-based, synthesised offline; ducked under the narration in mix.py.

SOUND EFFECTS
Synthesised in mix.py with numpy / core/audio/sfx.py: cuts, pops, slams, ticks, rings,
rises, chip clicks, arrow whooshes, room tone.

VOICE
Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george (en-us).

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1, OFL files in fonts/)
Inter Tight (display) · DM Mono (labels and HUD).

PHYSICS FACTS
Event horizon, spaghettification, gravitational time dilation, accretion-disk temperatures,
Hawking radiation and black-hole evaporation after standard general-relativity and
quantum-field descriptions (e.g. LIGO Scientific Collaboration and NASA public materials).
